{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures","id":1450321,"title":"Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-30T09:56:20-07:00","id":1450321,"title":"Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures","content":"I thought I'd make a separate thread for this, since it seems to be a particular sore spot.<br /> <br /> I never liked the old Frenzy mechanics. They were too all or nothing. And they resulted in scenes where your character just roleplayed being constipated while waiting to accumulate five successes on that Self-Control roll or to fail it. Just you standing there going &quot;uuuuh must...resist..frenzy!&quot; with an expression like you were on the toilet and hadn't eaten any fiber after a huge meal of red meat. It was bland. It was boring. It was not a fun mechanic.<br /> <br /> Whereas the Messy Critical/Bestial Failure mechanic has many fun results. It creates scenes that more closely resemble the moderate self-control failures that vampires in fiction seem to exhibit. For example, this scene in &quot;Fright Night&quot; can be perfectly explained in terms of messy crit/bestial failure results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=busozfENY0I\" data-code=\"busozfENY0I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/busozfENY0I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;A bouncer blocks your path. He says 'you want chicken, man, you go someplace else&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-&quot;I say 'out of my way' forcefully to intimidate him to move aside&quot;.<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Manipulation+Intimidation&quot;<br /> <br /> *Jerry Dandrige Player rolls a Bestial Failure*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the bouncer is not intimidated. He says 'move me', and his unbearable insolence causes you to gain the Harm Compulsion&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-&quot;I bare my fangs, activate my Eyes of the Beast and Protean Claws, and do a called shot to his jugular with my claws&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-*mentally notes that activating both the eyes and claws should take two rounds, but lets it slide for Rule of Cool's sake* &quot;Roll Strength+Brawl&quot;<br /> <br /> *Jerry Dandrige Player rolls, scoring four 10's.*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you land a devastating critical hit to his jugular. The bouncer goes down, mortally wounded. Another bouncer rushes in to help him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige player-&quot;I blood surge my Strength, pick him up by the throat, and throw him across the room.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Strength+Brawl&quot;<br /> <br /> *Jerry Dandrige player rolls, scoring a messy critical*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you lift him by the throat, crushing his windpipe in the process, and hurl him across the room. Everyone on the dancefloor panics and rushes for the door. In the chaos, you lose track of Amy&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't do that with the old all-of-nothing, you stand there with a massively constipated expression on your face waiting to succeed or fail on the extended self-control roll, rules.<br /> <br /> I adore this mechanic. It's been a &quot;OMG awesome where has this mechanic been all my life?? :-D&quot; experience for me both to play and run with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T11:05:09-07:00","id":1450330,"title":"","content":"Congratulations, you just described a blatant Masquerade breach, the rest of the session is now covering that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T11:13:20-07:00","id":1450332,"title":"","content":"ngl, jerry in your example is a fucking idiot, there was no reason to break the masquarade that hard","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T11:34:35-07:00","id":1450333,"title":"","content":"So, yeah, basically my response last time:<br /> <br /> It's not a bad result if you're trying to represent a certain kind of vampire and certain kinds of vampire fiction. It's a bad result for VtM, because as restated above, breaking the Masquerade like that has insanely serious consequences in the VtM setting. When people complain about the Messy Crit/Beastial Failure mechanics, this is something they think is a negative to the system: a bad set of rolls might make a cool cinematic moment, but when you return to the reality in which that vampire exists, they're now a wanted criminal that could easily have a death sentence waiting for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T17:15:45-07:00","id":1450375,"title":"","content":"I actually think in this example, the scene is not that bad of a masquerade breach. It's not hard to explain away. I've seen far, far worse.<br /> <br /> Dandrige killed the man with wolf claws. But it would most likely be explained away as a guy using a knife or some other weapon somehow smuggled into the club. People likely weren't even looking at the attack except the one guy who is now dead. Leon of course saw some weird stuff regarding Dandridge's looks, but assuming he survives he might not remember it, attribute it to stress or injury, or simply won't be believed by others. Depending on the specific results of the dead guy's throat, there may be some strange forensic evidence, but it'll likely just be attributed to an unknown weapon. Without doing anything to cover it up, this will likely just get attributed to a bouncer seeing a guy with a weapon in the club, shouting for Leon to back him up, getting killed by the knife guy, and Leon falling off the stairs as he attempted to stop the attacker. Police probably get a vague description of the &quot;attacker&quot; that could fit Dandridge as well as lots of other guys because when fights break out like this, people panic and run away, they aren't trying to get a good look at the attacker. I really don't see anything an ST or PCs would need to do to cover it up. Just lay low for a while.<br /> <br /> Certainly by sticking to the actions, but describing the scene a little bit differently than what we see in the cinematic portrayal (whose portrayal has different needs than that of an RPG game), it becomes ever less of an issue.<br /> <br /> As an ST, I would not be too concerned about this as an isolated incident (as opposed to a persistent pattern that would attract more attention). It wasn't the smartest play by Dandridge and the police will be looking for the &quot;knife guy&quot; for the immediate future, but considering the panic there actually isn't much evidence of the supernatural. I would actually prefer this than say the PC failing his frenzy roll and then attempting to kill everyone in the club who couldn't get away, which would be a disaster the game might not recover from.<br /> <br /> If this was the worst extent of masquerade breaches I've seen in game, I would have a much larger pool of players I'd be willing to play VtM with.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't play V5 so I don't know the rules of Bestial Failures. If it is anything like the old Botch rules, I could see why people don't like them, as every player I known that played the Storyteller System complains about the sheer frequency botches come up (as well as many other things, my gaming groups hold the opinion that we really like the setting but think the mechanics are terrible). If Bestial Failures crop up too often, it'd be the exact same problem with botches but worse. But as something that is an <i>alternative</i> to frenzy (hmm, rather than roll S-C, would you rather just take a Bestial Failure for the scene?), I'd give it a thumbs up. More options in resolving a scene is generally a good thing. But again, that's not a comment on the actual V5 mechanics which I don't know. Just going by the OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-30-2021, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T18:43:10-07:00","id":1450381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450330#post1450330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations, you just described a blatant Masquerade breach, the rest of the session is now covering that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that was our main problem when we tried it, most sessions devolved into cascading breaches and cover ups until the main plot had to be abandoned to deal with fixing random shit the dice threw at us while hoping it didn't get worse due to more random shit.<br /> <br /> So more unfunny farce than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T23:37:07-07:00","id":1450403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450381#post1450381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, that was our main problem when we tried it, most sessions devolved into cascading breaches and cover ups until the main plot had to be abandoned to deal with fixing random shit the dice threw at us while hoping it didn't get worse due to more random shit.<br /> <br /> So more unfunny farce than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Same here tbf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T02:26:41-07:00","id":1450418,"title":"","content":"I've wondered if it could be tied to Willpower expenditure like Imbalance in C20. E.g., if your temporary Willpower drops to one (or, if you like fewer Bestial Failures, 6-Self-Control), you have a Bestial Failure whenever you botch. Or maybe you pick up a Compulsion instead, and this activates automatically, rather than requiring a botch.<br /> <br /> But I also like Black Fox's idea that you can opt to take a Bestial Failure instead of rolling for Frenzy. It just means you'd need to be fairly consistent in requiring Frenzy checks or you have the same problem.<br /> <br /> Maybe the ExEss model for Limit Breaks works best of all: you can be subject to the Beast at a dramatically appropriate time and if everyone enjoys how you RP it, you gain a reward. In the ExEss KS manuscript, it's an extra 1xp, but you could maybe reward them with one WP point or something as well (or instead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:24:16-07:00","id":1450432,"title":"","content":"The C20 approach is pretty easy to slot in with Bestial Failures and the base V5 mechanics: the severity of a Bestial Failure is based on how much Aggravated Willpower damage you've taken. Among other things, it would also bring back a normal botch for non-vampire characters by having one for when you don't have an Aggravated Willpower damage.<br /> <br /> You can work in the carrot method with something like &quot;choose to upgrade a normal failure into a Bestial Failure, and convert all your current Aggravated Willpower damage to Superficial Willpower damage,&quot; as a way to encourage players to have their PCs cut lose emotionally, but have some say in it rather than it just being the dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T07:23:43-07:00","id":1450448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450432#post1450432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The C20 approach is pretty easy to slot in with Bestial Failures and the base V5 mechanics: the severity of a Bestial Failure is based on how much Aggravated Willpower damage you've taken. Among other things, it would also bring back a normal botch for non-vampire characters by having one for when you don't have an Aggravated Willpower damage.<br /> <br /> You can work in the carrot method with something like &amp;quot;choose to upgrade a normal failure into a Bestial Failure, and convert all your current Aggravated Willpower damage to Superficial Willpower damage,&amp;quot; as a way to encourage players to have their PCs cut lose emotionally, but have some say in it rather than it just being the dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that works. It's a pretty good incentive for a pretty punitive system (WP damage), so it balances that out a bit too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T11:41:42-07:00","id":1450473,"title":"","content":"The same scene using the old system:<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;A bouncer blocks your path. He says 'you want chicken, man, you go someplace else&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-&quot;I say 'out of my way' forcefully to try to intimidate him to move aside.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Manipulation plus Intimdation, difficultyyyyy, let's say, he's a big experienced bouncer, so let's say...8&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-*rolls 1, 1, 5, 5, 6, 8, 8* &quot;two successes...oh wait there's botches...&quot; *picks out 1's and 8's* &quot;failure&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the bouncer is not intimidated. He says 'move me!' with a challenging posture and tone, blocking your path again. It's frustrating and humiliating to have this insolent human challenging and blocking you, so give me a frenzy roll, difficultyyyy, let's say four.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-*rolls 1, 4, 5* &quot;I succeed. I clench my fists, say, 'must...resist..frenzy' under my breath, then I back off and..&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;actually you need to accumulate five successes on an extended roll to resist frenzy. So, it's next round, you are struggling with frenzy&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-&quot;oh, okay...um..&quot; *Dandrige Player mimes clenching his fists and having an expression like someone with with severe constipation trying to push out a HUGE shit &quot;I say 'must..resist..frenzy&quot; again and try again this round gettinnng&quot; *rolls 2, 3, 9* &quot;one more success&quot;<br /> <br /> Amy Brewster Player-*notices she doesn't have any much salsa left for her tortilla chips. Goes to the kitchen to get some more since this is going to take a while*<br /> <br /> Evil Ed Player-*texts on his phone*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the bouncer looks at you with an expression that is half bafflement, half horror. He says, 'man you a fuckin' weirdass nutjob'. He turns and shouts to another bouncer, 'Leon, help me kick this crazyass muthafuka outta the club!' &quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-*continues miming the constipated expression of his character as he attempts to resist frenzy* &quot;I keep trying to resist frenzy gettinggg...*rolls 3, 6, 6* two more successes. That's four total. Almost there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the first bouncer and Leon grab you by both arms and start dragging you towards the exit. The humiliation of being treated like a smelly peasant increases your difficulty to 8.&quot;<br /> <br /> Amy Brewster Player-*mixes in some shredded sharp chedder with her salsa and starts muching*<br /> <br /> Evil Ed Player-*continues texting on his phone*<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-&quot;crap. Come on, dice don't fail me now!&quot; *rolls 1, 5, 7, a botch* &quot;uh..can I spend a willpower point?&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you have to declare that before you roll. Okay, you botch your frenzy roll. Your character goes completely berzerk, he pops claws and it's almost like the end of 'American Werewolf In London'. He claws the first bouncer open from chin to crotch, and disembowls the second one, then he leaps on the nearest clubber and tears her head clean off. The entire club starts running for the door. You chase down the closest one and rack his back from shoulders to buttocks with both hands. You continue slaughtering people as the club empties. Some of the clubbers trample each other, leading to more deaths even among those you don't attack directly. After several minutes of this you come out of frenzy to find yourself surrounded by over a dozen bodies, most of them torn apart, a handful of them trampled by their fellow humans. You hear the sounds of police sirens.&quot;<br /> <br /> Amy Brewster Player-&quot;so are we gonna do my embrace scene soon? Evil Ed already got his.&quot; *dips a tortilla chip in salsa and munches it*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-31-2021, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T11:49:19-07:00","id":1450474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450473#post1450473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same scene using the old system:<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;A bouncer blocks your path. He says 'you want chicken, man, you go someplace else&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-&quot;I say 'out of my way' forcefully to try to intimidate him to move aside.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Manipulation plus Intimdation, difficultyyyyy, let's say, he's a big experienced bouncer, so let's say...8&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-*rolls 1, 1, 5, 5, 6, 8, 8* &quot;two successes...oh wait there's botches...&quot; *picks out 1's and 8's* &quot;failure&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the bouncer is not intimidated. He says 'move me!' with a challenging posture and tone, blocking your path again. It's frustrating and humiliating to have this insolent human challenging and blocking you, so give me a frenzy roll, difficultyyyy, let's say four.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-*rolls 1, 4, 5* &quot;I succeed. I clench my fists, say, 'must...resist..frenzy' under my breath, then I back off and..&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;actually you need to accumulate five successes on an extended roll to resist frenzy. So, it's next round, you are struggling with frenzy&quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-&quot;oh, okay...um..&quot; *Dandrige Player mimes clenching his fists and having an expression like someone with with severe constipation trying to push out a HUGE shit &quot;I say 'must..resist..frenzy&quot; again and try again this round gettinnng&quot; *rolls 2, 3, 9* &quot;one more success&quot;<br /> <br /> Amy Brewster Player-*notices she doesn't have any much salsa left for her tortilla chips. Goes to the kitchen to get some more since this is going to take a while*<br /> <br /> Evil Ed Player-*texts on his phone*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the bouncer looks at you with an expression that is half bafflement, half horror. He says, 'man you a fuckin' weirdass nutjob'. He turns and shouts to another bouncer, 'Leon, help me kick this crazyass muthafuka outta the club!' &quot;<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-*continues miming the constipated expression of his character as he attempts to resist frenzy* &quot;I keep trying to resist frenzy gettinggg...*rolls 3, 6, 6* two more successes. That's four total. Almost there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the first bouncer and Leon grab you by both arms and start dragging you towards the exit. The humiliation of being treated like a smelly peasant increases your difficulty to 8.&quot;<br /> <br /> Amy Brewster Player-*mixes in some shredded sharp chedder with her salsa and starts muching*<br /> <br /> Evil Ed Player-*continues texting on his phone*<br /> <br /> Jerry Dandrige Player-&quot;crap. Come on, dice don't fail me now!&quot; *rolls 1, 5, 7, a botch* &quot;uh..can I spend a willpower point?&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you have to declare that before you roll. Okay, you botch your frenzy roll. Your character goes completely berzerk, he pops claws and it's almost like the end of 'American Werewolf In London'. He claws the first bouncer open from chin to crotch, and disembowls the second one, then he leaps on the nearest clubber and tears her head clean off. The entire club starts running for the door. You chase down the closest one and rack his back from shoulders to buttocks with both hands. You continue slaughtering people as the club empties. Some of the clubbers trample each other, leading to more deaths even among those you don't attack directly. After several minutes of this you come out of frenzy to find yourself surrounded by over a dozen bodies, most of them torn apart, a handful of them trampled by their fellow humans. You hear the sounds of police sirens.&quot;<br /> <br /> Amy Brewster Player-&quot;so are we gonna do my embrace scene soon? Evil Ed already got his.&quot; *dips a tortilla chip in salsa and munches it*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> that happens at storytellers discretion, and is resisted by the characters attributes, messy/bestials happen at random, often multiple times per player per session, and have just as bad result. Oh and before people say 'roll less often' have they taken MMA training to be able to play physical capable characters? Or can socially awkward players please be allowed to use character skill, and thus rolls. rather than player skill, without the system punishing them for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-31-2021, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:10:53-07:00","id":1450478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450474#post1450474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that happens at storytellers discretion, and is resisted by the characters attributes, messy/bestials happen at random, often multiple times per player per session, and have just as bad result. Oh and before people say 'roll less often' have they taken MMA training to be able to play physical capable characters? Or can socially awkward players please be allowed to use character skill, and thus rolls. rather than player skill, without the system punishing them for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a GM, I also prefer to have everyone use the rolls because half the people who think they're not socially awkward are actually worse at RP (I presume we've all encountered those zero-self-awareness extroverted types at some point?) than the ones who do think they're socially awkward (and can be coaxed out a bit if they know the outcome isn't nearly as dependent on their self-evaluated ability to communicate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:40:23-07:00","id":1450485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450473#post1450473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same scene using the old system:</div> </div> </div> </div>Except of course, not, because the first example you wrote in roll results to get the scene as it played out (regardless of the probabilities or anything), and in your second example you wrote in dice results that didn't generate the scene (or as close to as possible).<br /> <br /> Also, you do realize that it's possible for the old rules to be not great, and the new rules to be not great? &quot;Here's an example of the old rules sucking in play, and an example of the new rules working perfectly in play,&quot; doesn't really address the totality of the experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T14:10:35-07:00","id":1450501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450485#post1450485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except of course, not, because the first example you wrote in roll results to get the scene as it played out (regardless of the probabilities or anything), and in your second example you wrote in dice results that didn't generate the scene (or as close to as possible).</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, you can't generate the scene using the old rules. The only other result I could have written was him eventually, slowly succeeding on his extended test frenzy roll, in which case Jerry Dandrige would have roleplayed the constipation face for as much as five rounds, been forced out of the club by the bouncers, and lost so much time that Amy and Charlie would have completely lost him and probably skipped town until dawn. The old Frenzy rules were too all-or-nothing, and extended rolls are inherently laborious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450485#post1450485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you do realize that it's possible for the old rules to be not great, and the new rules to be not great? &quot;Here's an example of the old rules sucking in play, and an example of the new rules working perfectly in play,&quot; doesn't really address the totality of the experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. But the new rules at least have the possibility of working perfectly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T15:18:13-07:00","id":1450511,"title":"","content":"Something that some don't take into consideration with bestial failures is that each non clan specific compulsion has different categories or ways to approach it. The examples being social, violent,and solitary. Sometimes the Beast wants to be the alpha putting the human or other vampire in their place/. It doesn't always have to come to physical violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T15:48:07-07:00","id":1450515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450501#post1450501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, you can't generate the scene using the old rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like a failed Frenzy check to me. The Beast takes over and kills those idiots humans that dare think they're a physical threat to him. I think you're forgetting that Frenzy's have different results for failures (which only means the Beast eliminates whatever was pissing the vampire off) and botch (where they go on a larger rampage).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...in which case Jerry Dandrige would have roleplayed the constipation face... </div> </div> </div>Which is just a hyperbolic bit of nonsense you're making up and doesn't help your case.<br /> <br /> V20 p. 298<br /> &quot;The character must score five successes to completely overcome the desires for violence, but even one success halts the frenzy temporarily. For each success below five, the character can<br /> resist the urge to frenzy for one turn. After this duration expires, the character may try again to gain extra successes and thus continue to resist the frenzy. Once five successes are acquired, over a longer or shorter period, the vampire resists the Beast\u2019s urges.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing about the character needing to just sit there making stupid faces. Every success is a full turn your character gets to act in control, not a turn you have to stand there doing nothing. If you want your PC to use their turns in control to deal with the bouncers with mundane skills or Disciplines, you're free to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's true. But the new rules at least have the possibility of working perfectly. </div> </div> </div>Well, when you house rule the old ones to make them worse, of course the new ones seem better for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T18:44:42-07:00","id":1450529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450515#post1450515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing about the character needing to just sit there making stupid faces. Every success is a full turn your character gets to act in control, not a turn you have to stand there doing nothing. If you want your PC to use their turns in control to deal with the bouncers with mundane skills or Disciplines, you're free to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>And worth noting is that, outside of combat a turn is variable and could be up to a minute depending on the situation. One minute or even 15 seconds to back the heck out of a situation you know is triggering your Beast is the difference between making sure that even if you ultimately fail you're throwing a tantrum in an empty alley and putting dents in a garbage bin and concrete/brick walls and going medieval on a bunch of innocent people.<br /> <br /> Its also something worth burning a willpower point on if you're in a situation where your frenzy could get someone killed and you're still humane enough that that matters to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T19:27:25-07:00","id":1450534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450529#post1450529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And worth noting is that, outside of combat a turn is variable and could be up to a minute depending on the situation. One minute or even 15 seconds to back the heck out of a situation you know is triggering your Beast is the difference between making sure that even if you ultimately fail you're throwing a tantrum in an empty alley and putting dents in a garbage bin and concrete/brick walls and going medieval on a bunch of innocent people.<br /> <br /> Its also something worth burning a willpower point on if you're in a situation where your frenzy could get someone killed and you're still humane enough that that matters to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's worth noting that even IN combat, a turn is variiable. It's a series of exchanges, it's not 'one turn is 3 seconds is one swing of the sword/shot of a gun' as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T04:14:33-07:00","id":1450569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450501#post1450501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, you can't generate the scene using the old rules. The only other result I could have written was him eventually, slowly succeeding on his extended test frenzy roll, in which case Jerry Dandrige would have roleplayed the constipation face for as much as five rounds, been forced out of the club by the bouncers, and lost so much time that Amy and Charlie would have completely lost him and probably skipped town until dawn. The old Frenzy rules were too all-or-nothing, and extended rolls are inherently laborious.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's true. But the new rules at least have the possibility of working perfectly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are several problems with the above example. Firstly, none of the other PCs are getting a turn while this encounter goes on, meaning they hang around waiting. That's just bad STing. <br /> <br /> Second, Virtue rolls are usually reflexive, so the PC could do something rather than just standing there looking like he's straining to defecate. You can then adjust the difficulty of the extended Self-Control roll based on the actions he takes (e.g., if he proceeds to batter the guy, I'd raise the difficulty; if he backs off and tries to remove himself from the situation, I'd reduce the difficulty).<br /> <br /> Also, if you know you're only rolling three dice and you don't want to fail, you'd spend the WP from the first roll to ensure you can't botch. When it comes to Frenzy rolls, you only take the risk when you're not in a very public location with lots of mortals around.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that a 'between Frenzy and cool' option is nice, but the example you gave is also a relatively skewed one.<br /> <br /> ETA: I stupidly didn't see the second page of comments, so I apologise for being late to the party! That's what happens when you try to post with the flu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-01-2021, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T11:12:23-07:00","id":1450613,"title":"","content":"The first example also doesn't even introduce the idea that there are other players sitting around. Consider that in the first example, there are seven exchanges between the ST and player... without any time spent on what anyone else is doing. But in the second example, two other players suddenly exist to be bored out of their minds after only four ST-player exchanges where everything is focused on one player.<br /> <br /> Apparently Messy Crits/Bestial Failures are so fun to everyone at the table, that the ST can completely forget two players exist for 30 minutes to deal with the scene, while those two players will sit there and be completely enraptured by the experience of doing nothing but watching someone else have fun.<br /> <br /> Or it's just a hyperbolic apples-to-oranges comparison that was never supposed to really be honest about the strengths and flaws in either system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T12:22:04-07:00","id":1450624,"title":"","content":"It's not that the other players aren't there, it's that the new system is so fast they don't have time to get bored. The first scene actually happening would only take slightly longer to play out than to read it.<br /> <br /> The second scene would take waayyyy longer to play out than to read. Because you're looking for ones and successes, then you're picking out the ones and successes, then you're checking for specialties and rerolling tens if a specialty applies, then you're picking out ones and successes again. Then once a combat starts, you're rolling initiative, then you're rolling Dex+Brawl, then you're picking out ones and successes, then you're checking if the Dex or Brawl specialty applies, if does. then you're rerolling tens, and you're picking out ones and successes, then you're doing a damage roll, then you're picking ones and successes, then you're checking if the Strength specialty applies to this damage, if does, you're rerolling tens, then you're picking out ones and successes. That scene might actually have taken an hour to play out if the ST decided to actually roll for the club slaughter instead of narrating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T12:44:41-07:00","id":1450628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450624#post1450624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that the other players aren't there, it's that the new system is so fast they don't have time to get bored. The first scene actually happening would only take slightly longer to play out than to read it.<br /> <br /> The second scene would take waayyyy longer to play out than to read. Because you're looking for ones and successes, then you're picking out the ones and successes, then you're checking for specialties and rerolling tens if a specialty applies, then you're picking out ones and successes again. Then once a combat starts, you're rolling initiative, then you're rolling Dex+Brawl, then you're picking out ones and successes, then you're checking if the Dex or Brawl specialty applies, if does. then you're rerolling tens, and you're picking out ones and successes, then you're doing a damage roll, then you're picking ones and successes, then you're checking if the Strength specialty applies to this damage, if does, you're rerolling tens, then you're picking out ones and successes. That scene might actually have taken an hour to play out if the ST decided to actually roll for the club slaughter instead of narrating it.</div> </div> </div> </div>you're entitled to your opinion but your examples to prove your point are shit mate holy fuck. your example you just gave proves that V5 has faster combat (not even that cuz you emitted combat from your first example) instead of the merit of hunger dice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T14:07:13-07:00","id":1450639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450321-messy-criticals-and-bestial-failures?p=1450624#post1450624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that the other players aren't there, it's that the new system is so fast they don't have time to get bored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so what you're claiming that all the players being completely ignored for an hour while the ST just focuses on one player are simply blinded by the speed of how fast the system is that they stop caring that they've still been ignored for an hour. Gotcha.<br /> <br /> And I thought you were trying to make the case that Messy Crits and Bestial Failures generate better scenes, not that combat is faster in V5 (of course, you know, even if you cut V20 to two rolls per attack instead of four, V5's only faster because there's a cap of 3 rounds of combat not because the combat mechanics actually result in fast combat resolution).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first scene actually happening would only take slightly longer to play out than to read it. </div> </div> </div>Because you're stacking the deck to make it an unfair comparison rather than trying to actually do an apples-to-apples thing. In the first example everyone seems to have the rules memorized perfectly, instantly interprets the dice, and the ST instantly knows exactly which results they want to have, while the second example everyone is fumbling around even with basic stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because you're looking for ones and successes, then you're picking out the ones and successes, then you're checking for specialties and rerolling tens if a specialty applies, then you're picking out ones and successes again. </div> </div> </div>V20 just has specialty 10s count as two successes rather than rerolling.<br /> <br /> Beyond that... you do realize that figuring out if you have a Messy Crit or Bestial Failure involves... count up 1s and 10s and comparing them, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then once a combat starts... </div> </div> </div>You do realize your second example had the other players bored before combat started, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That scene might actually have taken an hour to play out if the ST decided to actually roll for the club slaughter instead of narrating it. </div> </div> </div>How is that really any different for the first example?<br /> <br /> And I could run that in 10 minutes with my experienced players with full combat and all the rolling. The entire scene. I've done far more complex scenes (because the other players were doing stuff too) in that time with the X20 system without cutting out combat rolls.<br /> <br /> The older rules are needlessly clunky, sure. I'd love to see better ones, but that doesn't mean you're proving anything in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}